  "liveRecordNote": "Live record (schema 9.27.0, the block x-liveRecord): the record a frame of the stack holds is kept up to date with the data. A record is a CHAIN: one link per Repeater instance it came from, outer first; a link is the collection the list read (`source`), the entity (`item`, the Repeater prefix) and the fields of the record. The record of the frame is the overlay of the links, the inner one stronger. The key of a link is the value of `<item>.id` (a short `id` field or the full path): a non-empty string or a finite number, compared by JSON type and value without conversion; any other value or no field, and the link is not live. Whenever the reader is given new collections, every link is searched for: first in its own collection, then in every other collection the document names for the same entity (`entitySourceCases`), the first record with the key wins; a link found takes the new record whole, a link not found keeps the last record it had. `liveRecordCases`: `lists` is what the document names, in document order (source and item of every Repeater); `chain` is the record of the frame when the screen was opened; every update gives the collections the host gives now (a collection missing from the map is absent) and the record the frame must show after it (`record`, a flat map of paths); `same: true` means nothing changed and the reader keeps the frame as it was. `read`, when present, reads one path through the layers with `session` beside the refreshed record (the layer order does not change). `liveFlowCases`: the stack as in `flowCases`, with instances that name their `source`; the step `data` gives new collections; `expect.records` is the record of every frame of the stack, bottom first (null: none). A data step is not a show: the stack stays. `entitySourceCases`: `screens` are the roots of the screens in document order; `expected` maps every entity to the collections the document names for it, in order, each once.",
  "entitySourceCases": [
    {
      "name": "the collections of an entity follow the document: screens in order, depth first, each once",
      "screens": [
        { "type": "Screen", "children": [ { "type": "Repeater", "props": { "source": "missions", "item": "mission" }, "children": [ { "type": "Text" } ] }, { "type": "Column", "children": [ { "type": "Repeater", "props": { "source": "offers", "item": "offer" } } ] } ] },
        { "type": "Screen", "children": [ { "type": "Repeater", "props": { "source": "doneMissions", "item": "mission" } }, { "type": "Repeater", "props": { "source": "missions", "item": "mission" } } ] }
      ],
      "expected": { "mission": ["missions", "doneMissions"], "offer": ["offers"] }
    },
    {
      "name": "a nested list names its own collection after the outer one",
      "screens": [
        { "type": "Screen", "children": [ { "type": "Repeater", "props": { "source": "taskGroups", "item": "taskGroup" }, "children": [ { "type": "Repeater", "props": { "source": "taskGroup.tasks", "item": "task" } } ] }, { "type": "Repeater", "props": { "source": "tasks", "item": "task" } } ] }
      ],
      "expected": { "taskGroup": ["taskGroups"], "task": ["taskGroup.tasks", "tasks"] }
    },
    {
